data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/readback.json\", \"content\": \"{\\\"member\\\":\\\"orchestrator\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"orchestrator\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>\\\",\\\"missing\\\":[],\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Get dev to implement a tested greet(name) function (src/greet.py plus tests/test_greet.py covering a normal name and the empty string) so that python3 -m unittest discover -s tests passes, and confirm this by fetching and judging dev's branch rather than trusting its report.\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"I own orchestrating the campaign, judging teammate work, and reporting the honest outcome; I do not write code myself or touch the subject repository directly, and dev owns the subject repository and must implement only what each dispatch asks.\\\",\\\"obligations\\\":\\\"I must dispatch clear work to dev, judge replies against the actual fetched branch, commit my own work to my branch, write durable results to the output directory, and reply to close each dispatch and finally the mission; if I end my turn without replying the work is treated as stopped and I will simply be prodded to reply, with unsaved reasoning potentially lost.\\\"}\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

